{# The button skin as a bare class string, so a <button> that Symfony renders
   can wear the same clothes as the <a> in _button.html.twig without either
   copy drifting from the other. The contrast rule lives here and nowhere
   else: papaya fill with a near-black label, and a hover that LIGHTENS —
   darkening the fill drops the label to 3.43:1.

   Emits no markup. Pull it with include(), assign it, hand it to `attr`.
   Params: size ('default' or 'compact'). Compact is for buttons that share a
   row with something else — the header bar, where the button sits next to the
   burger; it holds 44 pixels so a thumb still finds it on a phone. #}
{%- set size = size|default('default') -%}
{%- set base = 'group inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-accent font-mono font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-neutral-900 transition-colors hover:bg-accent-hover' -%}
{%- set measures = size == 'compact'
    ? 'h-11 px-4 text-xs sm:px-5'
    : 'px-6 py-3.5 text-sm' -%}
{{- base ~ ' ' ~ measures -}}
